# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the D+/door-2 concurrent-read design.
#
# Usage:  TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=src/tsan.sup" ./src/valkey-server ...
# Build:  make SANITIZER=thread
#
# PURPOSE: scope out the report classes that are BY DESIGN or that TSan
# cannot model, so that any NEW report is actionable signal. Each entry
# must carry its justification; do not add entries to silence a report
# you have not root-caused.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Class 1: seqlock speculative reads (BY DESIGN).
# dplusSpeculateBatch executes GETs on IO threads by reading hashtable
# buckets, entry keys, and robj values WITHOUT locks, racing main's writers
# (insert/moveEntry/rehashEntry/dbSetValue/memset) by construction. Torn or
# stale reads are expected and discarded: the sharded seqlock version check
# (dplusValidateAndReply) rejects any read that overlapped a mutation, and
# entry/table memory lifetime is guaranteed by quiescence-deferred
# reclamation (limbo lists), verified by ASan and the expiry-race gauntlet.
# Every by-design racy read has dplusSpeculateBatch in its stack, so this
# single entry scopes the whole class. True bugs in this path are covered
# by: seqlock validation itself, ASan legs, the V4 differential fuzzer,
# and ownership.tcl.
race:dplusSpeculateBatch

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Class 2: owned-client handshake (FENCE-ORDERED; TSan limitation).
# The door-2 owned-client handshake (io_read_state / io_write_state /
# flag.pending_write) uses volatile fields ordered by explicit
# atomic_thread_fence acquire/release pairs (DOOR2_RELEASE_OWNED_READ /
# DOOR2_RELEASE_OWNED_WRITE + the acquire in the worker dispatch guard).
# TSan does NOT model standalone fences, so it reports these as races even
# though the publications are ordered. The two functions below are the
# main-side consumers/publishers of the handshake. NOTE: this is the
# weakest suppression in the file — a genuine new race in these functions
# would be hidden from TSan; the V4 differential fuzzer and ownership.tcl
# are the compensating detectors for this surface.
race:processClientIOWriteDone
race:ioThreadWriteToClient

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Class 4: per-thread memory accounting aggregate (UPSTREAM DESIGN).
# zmalloc maintains a plain size_t counter per thread (used_memory_thread[i],
# each written only by its owning thread) and zmalloc_used_memory() sums all
# slots with plain reads from whichever thread asks (main via INFO/maxmemory,
# BIO via lazyfree accounting). The aggregate is intentionally imprecise --
# a torn/stale read changes a statistic, never control flow correctness, and
# aligned 8-byte loads don't tear on supported targets. This is inherited
# upstream valkey design (predates door-2), reproduced on the unmodified
# base commit 89e774674 under unit/lazyfree; converting the array to relaxed
# atomics is an upstream conversation, not a D+ fix. Root-caused Sep 4 2026
# (Phase 1 S1.6 sanitizer leg).
race:zmalloc_used_memory

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Class 5: owned-client read-handshake surface (PRE-EXISTING REPORT STORM --
# REAL CLASS, DEDICATED AUDIT PENDING, NOT ALL BENIGN). Under the
# instrumented ownership suite, TSan reports 22 distinct race locations on
# the UNMODIFIED base commit 89e774674 (evidence: /tmp/base-races.txt sweep
# Sep 4 2026): cross-thread fd registration vs the F13 unlocked sweep
# (aeCreateFileEvent/connSocketSetReadHandler/connIncrRefs), SPSC
# inbox/outbox accessors (spscEnqueue/IsEmpty/IsFull), query-buffer handoff
# (readToQueryBuf/parseMultibulk/readQueryFromClient), and D+ stats
# aggregation. This is the same fence-ordered surface Class 2 documents as
# TSan-unmodellable, PLUS genuinely unlocked windows that need their own
# audit -- tracked as the Phase 1 follow-up 'owned-client handshake TSan
# audit' in the lane tasks. Suppressed as a class so NEW keyspace-protocol
# races (the Phase 1 surface, verified TSan-clean on expire/string/keyspace/
# lazyfree suites) stay actionable. aePoll/clientsCron/sdsIncrLen appear
# only under the battery's parked-reader scenarios (hooks absent on base --
# provenance unverifiable) and are provisionally classed here.
race:aeCreateFileEvent
race:aeDeleteFileEvent
race:aePoll
race:aeSetDontWait
race:beforeNextClient
race:clientsCron
race:connIncrRefs
race:connSocketEventHandler
race:connSocketRead
race:connSocketSetReadHandler
race:connSocketSetWriteHandler
race:dplusAggregateStats
race:dplusConsumeSpeculated
race:dplusDoorbellRings
race:dplusInfoString
race:invoke_callback
race:ioThreadReadQueryFromClient
race:parseMultibulk
race:readQueryFromClient
race:readToQueryBuf
race:sdsIncrLen
race:spscEnqueue
race:spscIsEmpty
race:spscIsFull
race:trySendReadToIOThreads

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Class 6: module-GIL vs io_threads_mutex order inversion (UPSTREAM DESIGN).
# Init acquires GIL -> per-thread mutex (createIOThread); the event loop
# acquires per-thread mutex (held across sleep for inactive threads) -> GIL
# (afterSleep). Formal cycle, but both edges are main-thread-only: IO
# threads never take the GIL, so the cycle cannot close across threads.
# Reproduced 6x on unmodified base (Sep 4 2026). Upstream lineage
# (io-threads pause/resume + module GIL both predate door-2).
deadlock:createIOThread
deadlock:moduleAcquireGIL

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Class 3: crash-report path (best-effort by intent).
# The sigsegv handler's crash dump calls signal-unsafe logging on purpose
# (last-gasp diagnostics). These reports only appear once the process is
# already crashing — the crash itself is the actionable signal.
signal:sigsegvHandler
# DEBUG STACKTRACES / watchdog stack collection: threads_mngr delivers a
# signal to every thread and the handler walks/symbolizes stacks (malloc in
# dl machinery) -- deliberately best-effort diagnostics, upstream lineage.
signal:collect_stacktrace_data
signal:invoke_callback
signal:writeStacktraces
signal:printCrashReport
signal:serverLogRaw
signal:logServerInfo
signal:logModulesInfo
signal:logConfigDebugInfo
signal:logRegisters
signal:logStackContent
signal:doFastMemoryTest
